# 43 — Extend Astrid beyond video with image, 3D and writing editors

**Start:** [Astrid development skill](../../skills/astrid-dev/SKILL.md) and [shared run contract](../../skills/astrid-dev-shared/run-contract.md). [Inputs](inputs.md) · [Tasks](tasks.md). The [catalog](../index.md) owns priority, status and owner.

**Vision gaps:** [LS-004 — Extend Astrid beyond video with image, 3D and writing editors](../../vision/gaps/LS-004-cross-modal-foundations.md) (primary).

## Goal and scope

Establish powerful, deeply extensible image, 3D and writing editor foundations so independent contributors can extend Astrid across modalities rather than only video.

**Included:** Longer-term staged foundations: a strong editable image surface first, then native 3D editing and writing surfaces, each with agent/tool extension, saved projects and real creator work.

**Boundary:** Don't attempt full pro-suite parity in one project. Split implementation into independent modality plans once scoped and owned.

## What this builds on

[Plan 24 portable components](../24-liquid-workspace/plan.md), [Plan 45 component connections](../45-component-connections/plan.md) and [Plan 17 extensions](../17-vibecomfy-extensibility/plan.md). These are foundations to verify at current source revisions, not proof of a deployed result. Prefer reusing them over inventing another runtime or state owner.

## Proposed sequence

1. Map actual cross-modal creator jobs and reusable editor/agent/data contracts.
2. Build and validate a useful extendable image editor foundation.
3. Validate a native 3D editor foundation reusing shared primitives.
4. Validate a writing editor foundation and show one independent extension without forking core.

## Interfaces and handoff

Before product work, pin actual accepted base/donor revisions, implementation owners and dependencies. Consume existing pack/component/project contracts; produce a tested contract or working artifact and link exact product PRs. Never infer authorization from a draft.

## Completion

Validate a writing editor foundation and show one independent extension without forking core. Record integrated candidate identity, real creator/agent outcomes and meaningful negative cases. Completion does not automatically close the associated vision gap.

**Authorization:** Draft, unassigned, queued. Owner decision and focused checks are required before implementation.
